<Base title="The technical notebook — Clement"><section class="page-intro"><a class="text-link" href="/projects/">← All projects</a><h1>A notebook built<br/>for <em>technical ideas.</em></h1><p>The website you are reading is also a small, inspectable project.</p></section><div class="prose standalone-prose"><h2>Writing comes first</h2><p>Astro generates a static page for every Markdown or MDX entry. Newsreader gives long-form prose room to breathe; Manrope handles the interface; IBM Plex Mono keeps code and metadata distinct.</p><h2>Tools for explanation</h2><p>Shiki highlights code at build time. KaTeX renders equations. MDX supports reusable components, including the interactive Signal Lab and Mermaid diagrams. Each note gets a table of contents from its headings.</p><h2>Small by default</h2><p>Navigation and article text work without JavaScript. Search, theme switching, code copying, diagrams, and the interactive examples progressively enhance the pages that need them. Fonts are served from the same site.</p><h2>Publishing</h2><p>GitHub Actions checks and builds the site, then publishes the static output to GitHub Pages. The repository includes the authoring guide, locked dependencies, and checks for internal links and essential article features.</p><a href="https://github.com/poytaytoy/poytaytoy.github.io">Browse the source on GitHub ↗</a></div></Base>
